{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRy5JznurkmiNsYKZ2Ky","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are now sent through `Analytics.capture` on the registration and offers screens. Event and property names are unchanged. `flutter analyze` and the format check pass. A temporary widget test with a mocked PostHog channel passed all four checks. I removed that test afterwards, so the change stays within the two screen files. Nothing is committed; the write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n- **Email and phone \"started\":** fire once per screen, on the first edit, using a flag on the screen state. Per-keystroke `onChanged` would have fired once per character.\n- **Loan amount:** fires from `onChangeEnd`, once per drag, with the rounded amount.\n- **Terms:** fires when the box is ticked on, not when it is cleared.\n- **Continue:** fires before navigating, with `amount` and `terms`.\n- **Offers scroll:** fires from `ScrollEndNotification` around the list, with `offset` set to the scroll position.\n\nI applied three parts of the colleague's note: the once-per-visit flags, `onChangeEnd` for the slider, and `ScrollEndNotification` for scrolling. The focus-lost and tap-guard parts don't apply because no spec event needs them. I also did not run a debug build against PostHog, since that would send events to an external service.\n\nDecisions to check, also listed in `ANSWER.md`:\n- \"Once per visit\" means once per screen state. Going back from offers doesn't re-fire the \"started\" events.\n- `offset` is the scroll position, not the distance moved. The spec's \"how far they scrolled\" could mean either.\n\n`lib/analytics.dart` still has the placeholder key `phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI`, so nothing reaches PostHog until CI injects the real key. That was already true before this change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1012,"cache_read_input_tokens":52232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1012},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ad94870-3c61-4453-91aa-26892d809584","uuid":"256277af-2f5e-4576-9164-5ea3b288ecdd","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:39:31.951Z","request_id":"req_011CgRy5JjR1RNYLzZ8XbtCz"}
